@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il06-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il06-period`
IMPORT `nii-s1-basic-amount`
IMPORT `nii-s65-interpretation`
IMPORT `nii-s66-entitlement`
IMPORT `nii-s67-count-of-children`
IMPORT `nii-s68-amount`
IMPORT `nii-il06-published-figures`
IMPORT `nii-il06-family-on-a-day`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for row IL-06 (National Insurance Law ss 65-68), by fid-il-06.
--
-- Every expected value below was decided from the Hebrew source BEFORE this author opened any
-- .l4 file or NOTES.md, and is recorded with its licence in DECIDED-ANSWERS.md (finished
-- 2026-10-06 15:03:48 UTC). Each assertion carries that file's scenario id (A1, B4, C10 …).
-- No expected value was taken from the encoder's tests or from an evaluation. An assertion that
-- fails is a finding; it is left failing and discussed in INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md.
--
-- Figures: "chosen" = the three basic amounts printed in s 1 (2) itself, 150 / 188 / 140,
-- chosen as an input. "published" = the encoding's own module of NII figures, which this
-- author checked independently against the NII table fetched 2026-10-06 14:59:55 UTC (sha256
-- f873d1ef…1aec); the E3 assertions are that check.
--
-- Defaults (DECIDED-ANSWERS, "Defaults"): a parent is insured under s 65(a)(2) (a resident, not
-- insured under Chapter 11, not a housewife); no s 121B income; no Income Support or
-- maintenance payment; each child is the parent's own natural child, unmarried, in Israel,
-- under 18.

§ `Independent tests`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      ch11 IS A BOOLEAN
      housewife IS A BOOLEAN
      resident IS A BOOLEAN
      absentBeyond IS A BOOLEAN
      formerly IS A BOOLEAN
      addtax IS A BOOLEAN
      incsupp IS A BOOLEAN
      maint IS A BOOLEAN
      manywomen IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A person`
`ind person` n ch11 housewife resident absentBeyond formerly addtax incsupp maint manywomen MEANS
    `A person` WITH
        `name`                                                                                     IS n
        `insured under Chapter 11`                                                                 IS ch11
        `a housewife as defined in section 238`                                                    IS housewife
        `resident in Israel`                                                                       IS resident
        `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`                                IS absentBeyond
        `formerly insured`                                                                         IS formerly
        `income chargeable to additional tax under section 121B of the Income Tax Ordinance`      IS addtax
        `paid, for the month, a benefit under the Income Support Law`                             IS incsupp
        `paid, for the month, a monthly payment under the Maintenance (Assurance of Payment) Law` IS maint
        `children by more than one woman`                                                          IS manywomen

-- s 65(a)(2): resident, not insured under Chapter 11, not a housewife.
GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`ind resident` n MEANS `ind person` n FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Neither limb: not resident, not insured under Chapter 11.
GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`ind nonresident` n MEANS `ind person` n FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- s 65(a)(1): insured under Chapter 11, not a housewife (and not resident, so limb (2) is not what makes the person insured).
GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`ind ch11` n MEANS `ind person` n TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`ind resident absent beyond a reasonable absence` n MEANS `ind person` n FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`ind resident with additional tax` n MEANS `ind person` n FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`ind resident on income support` n MEANS `ind person` n FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`ind resident on maintenance` n MEANS `ind person` n FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`ind resident housewife` n MEANS `ind person` n FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`ind formerly insured` n MEANS `ind person` n FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`ind resident man with children by several women` n MEANS `ind person` n FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

-- Parent entries in a child's record.
GIVEN n IS A STRING, st IS A `Standing to the child`, fm IS A `Father or mother`, w IS A BOOLEAN, sp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`ind entry` n st fm w sp MEANS
    `A parent in a child's record` WITH
        `name of the person`            IS n
        `standing`                      IS st
        `father or mother`              IS fm
        `the child is with this person` IS w
        `support proven`                IS sp

GIVEN n IS A STRING, w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`ind natural father` n w MEANS `ind entry` n `the child's natural parent` `the child's father` w FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING, w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`ind natural mother` n w MEANS `ind entry` n `the child's natural parent` `the child's mother` w FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING, w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`ind adoptive father` n w MEANS `ind entry` n `the child's adoptive parent` `the child's father` w FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING, w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`ind adoptive mother` n w MEANS `ind entry` n `the child's adoptive parent` `the child's mother` w FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING, w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`ind step-father` n w MEANS `ind entry` n `the child's step-parent` `the child's father` w FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING, w IS A BOOLEAN, sp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`ind supporting grandmother` n w sp MEANS `ind entry` n `a person who is not the child's parent` `the child's mother` w sp

-- Children.
GIVEN n IS A STRING, dob IS A DATE, married IS A BOOLEAN, ab IS A MAYBE `An absence from Israel`, inst IS A BOOLEAN, ps IS A LIST OF `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A `A child`
`ind child full` n dob married ab inst ps MEANS
    `A child` WITH
        `name`                                         IS n
        `date of birth`                                IS dob
        `married`                                      IS married
        `absence from Israel`                          IS ab
        `the Institute regards the child as in Israel` IS inst
        `parents`                                      IS ps

GIVEN n IS A STRING, dob IS A DATE, ps IS A LIST OF `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A `A child`
`ind child` n dob ps MEANS `ind child full` n dob FALSE NOTHING FALSE ps

-- A child of the single mother "P", with her.
GIVEN n IS A STRING, dob IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A child`
`ind P's child` n dob MEANS `ind child` n dob (LIST `ind natural mother` "P" TRUE)

GIVEN l IS A DATE, r IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `An absence from Israel`
`ind absence` l r MEANS `An absence from Israel` WITH
    `the day the child left Israel`        IS l
    `the day the child returned to Israel` IS r

GIVEN d  IS A DATE
      ps IS A LIST OF `A person`
      cs IS A LIST OF `A child`
GIVETH A `A family on a day`
`ind family` d ps cs MEANS `A family on a day` WITH
    `the day`      IS d
    `the persons`  IS ps
    `the children` IS cs

-- The single mother "P" with the children given, on a day.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, p IS A `A person`, cs IS A LIST OF `A child`
GIVETH A `A family on a day`
`ind single` d p cs MEANS `ind family` d (LIST p) cs

GIVETH A DATE
`ind usual day` MEANS YMD 2026 3 1

GIVETH A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
`ind chosen` MEANS `The basic amounts for the child allowance` WITH
    `under paragraph (2)(a)` IS 150
    `under paragraph (2)(b)` IS 188
    `under paragraph (2)(c)` IS 140

§§ `Reading the answer`

GIVEN f IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
`ind at chosen` f MEANS `the child allowance of each person, in` f `, at` `ind chosen`

GIVEN f IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
`ind at published` f MEANS `the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` f

GIVEN n IS A STRING, r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`
`ind answers for` n r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN LEFT p   THEN EMPTY
    WHEN RIGHT as THEN filter (GIVEN a YIELD a's `name of the person` EQUALS n) as

-- The person's monthly total, before rounding; NOTHING if the facts were rejected.
GIVEN n IS A STRING, r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`ind total` n r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN LEFT p   THEN NOTHING
    WHEN RIGHT as THEN JUST (sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD `the total, before rounding, of` (a's `the answer`)) (`ind answers for` n r)))

GIVEN a IS A `The child allowance of a person for the month`
GIVETH A LIST OF `The allowance for a child in the count`
`ind lines of` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `a monthly child allowance` ls THEN ls
    OTHERWISE EMPTY

GIVEN n IS A STRING, r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A LIST OF `The allowance for a child in the count`
`ind lines` n r MEANS concat (map (GIVEN a YIELD `ind lines of` (a's `the answer`)) (`ind answers for` n r))

GIVEN n IS A STRING, r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ind count` n r MEANS count (`ind lines` n r)

-- s 68(a)/(b) amount of each line, in the count's order.
GIVEN n IS A STRING, r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`ind per child` n r MEANS map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b), before rounding`) (`ind lines` n r)

GIVEN n IS A STRING, r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`ind supplements` n r MEANS map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `the supplement under section 68(c), before rounding`) (`ind lines` n r)

GIVEN n IS A STRING, r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`ind child names` n r MEANS map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `name of the child`) (`ind lines` n r)

GIVEN n IS A STRING, r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A LIST OF `The provision that fixes the allowance for a child`
`ind provisions` n r MEANS map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `the provision`) (`ind lines` n r)

-- Is the person's answer exactly this kind of "no allowance"?
GIVEN n IS A STRING, r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`), k IS A `The child allowance of a person for the month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind answer is` n r k MEANS any (GIVEN a YIELD a's `the answer` EQUALS k) (`ind answers for` n r)

-- In whose count is the child (s 67)?
GIVEN f IS A `A family on a day`, c IS A `A child`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`ind whose count` f c MEANS `s 67 — the insured parent in whose count, in` f `, is` c

-- The same, forced to a plain string, so that a refusal sitting inside a JUST is reached
-- (a #ASSERT REFUSED on a MAYBE might stop at the JUST; phrasebook 11.8).
GIVEN f IS A `A family on a day`, c IS A `A child`
GIVETH A STRING
`ind whose count, forced` f c MEANS
    CONSIDER `ind whose count` f c
    WHEN JUST s  THEN s
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "(in no count)"

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`ind published` d MEANS
    LIST a's `under paragraph (2)(a)`, a's `under paragraph (2)(b)`, a's `under paragraph (2)(c)`
    WHERE a MEANS `the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` d

GIVEN r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind rejected` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN LEFT p   THEN TRUE
    WHEN RIGHT as THEN FALSE

§§ `A — entitlement: s 66 and the definitions it relies on`

`ind A1 child` MEANS `ind P's child` "C1" (YMD 2021 1 1)

-- A1 / A6: single insured parent, one child aged 5: 150.
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind resident` "P") (LIST `ind A1 child`))) EQUALS JUST 150
-- A2: not insured: no allowance, and for the stated reason.
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind nonresident` "P") (LIST `ind A1 child`))) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `ind answer is` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind nonresident` "P") (LIST `ind A1 child`))) `no child allowance, not being an insured parent`
-- A3: insured under Chapter 11 (limb (1)).
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind ch11` "P") (LIST `ind A1 child`))) EQUALS JUST 150
-- A4: a resident on a temporary absence the authorised employee thinks reasonable: insured.
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind resident` "P") (LIST `ind A1 child`))) EQUALS JUST 150
-- A5: s 121B income: no allowance, and for that reason.
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind resident with additional tax` "P") (LIST `ind A1 child`))) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `ind answer is` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind resident with additional tax` "P") (LIST `ind A1 child`))) `no child allowance, being an insured parent with income chargeable to additional tax`

-- A7: the only child is 17 and married: not a "child".
#ASSERT `ind count` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind resident` "P") (LIST `ind child full` "M17" (YMD 2008 6 1) TRUE NOTHING FALSE (LIST `ind natural mother` "P" TRUE)))) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind resident` "P") (LIST `ind child full` "M17" (YMD 2008 6 1) TRUE NOTHING FALSE (LIST `ind natural mother` "P" TRUE)))) EQUALS JUST 0

-- A8: two children 17 and 7: 338; once the elder marries, the younger is first: 150.
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind resident` "P") (LIST `ind P's child` "E" (YMD 2008 6 1), `ind P's child` "Y" (YMD 2018 6 1)))) EQUALS JUST 338
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind resident` "P") (LIST `ind child full` "E" (YMD 2008 6 1) TRUE NOTHING FALSE (LIST `ind natural mother` "P" TRUE), `ind P's child` "Y" (YMD 2018 6 1)))) EQUALS JUST 150

-- A9: insured step-father S; the natural parents are not insured; the child lives with S.
`ind A9 child` MEANS `ind child` "K" (YMD 2016 1 1) (LIST `ind step-father` "S" TRUE, `ind natural mother` "NM" FALSE, `ind natural father` "NF" FALSE)
`ind A9 family` MEANS `ind family` `ind usual day` (LIST `ind resident` "S", `ind nonresident` "NM", `ind nonresident` "NF") (LIST `ind A9 child`)
#ASSERT `ind whose count` `ind A9 family` `ind A9 child` EQUALS JUST "S"
#ASSERT `ind total` "S" (`ind at chosen` `ind A9 family`) EQUALS JUST 150

-- A10: single insured adoptive mother.
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind resident` "P") (LIST `ind child` "AC" (YMD 2016 1 1) (LIST `ind adoptive mother` "P" TRUE)))) EQUALS JUST 150

-- A11 / A12: insured grandmother G who supported her grandchild (proved / not proved); the parents are not insured.
GIVEN sp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A child`
`ind A11 child` sp MEANS `ind child` "GC" (YMD 2016 1 1) (LIST `ind supporting grandmother` "G" TRUE sp, `ind natural mother` "NM" FALSE, `ind natural father` "NF" FALSE)
GIVEN sp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A family on a day`
`ind A11 family` sp MEANS `ind family` `ind usual day` (LIST `ind resident` "G", `ind nonresident` "NM", `ind nonresident` "NF") (LIST `ind A11 child` sp)
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind A11 family` TRUE) (`ind A11 child` TRUE) EQUALS JUST "G"
#ASSERT `ind total` "G" (`ind at chosen` (`ind A11 family` TRUE)) EQUALS JUST 150
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind A11 family` FALSE) (`ind A11 child` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ind total` "G" (`ind at chosen` (`ind A11 family` FALSE)) EQUALS JUST 0

-- A13: a child abroad (left 2025-06-01, still away, no Institute decision): not counted.
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind resident` "P") (LIST `ind child full` "AB" (YMD 2016 1 1) FALSE (JUST (`ind absence` (YMD 2025 6 1) NOTHING)) FALSE (LIST `ind natural mother` "P" TRUE)))) EQUALS JUST 0

§§ `B — the count: s 67`

GIVEN fw IS A BOOLEAN, mw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A child`
`ind FM child` fw mw MEANS `ind child` "K" (YMD 2016 1 1) (LIST `ind natural father` "F" fw, `ind natural mother` "M" mw)

GIVEN fp IS A `A person`, mp IS A `A person`, fw IS A BOOLEAN, mw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A family on a day`
`ind FM family` fp mp fw mw MEANS `ind family` `ind usual day` (LIST fp, mp) (LIST `ind FM child` fw mw)

-- B1-B4: both natural parents insured.
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident` "F") (`ind resident` "M") TRUE TRUE) (`ind FM child` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST "F"
#ASSERT `ind total` "F" (`ind at chosen` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident` "F") (`ind resident` "M") TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS JUST 150
#ASSERT `ind total` "M" (`ind at chosen` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident` "F") (`ind resident` "M") TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident` "F") (`ind resident` "M") FALSE TRUE) (`ind FM child` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST "M"
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident` "F") (`ind resident` "M") TRUE FALSE) (`ind FM child` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST "F"
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident` "F") (`ind resident` "M") FALSE FALSE) (`ind FM child` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST "F"
-- B5: only F insured, child with both.
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident` "F") (`ind nonresident` "M") TRUE TRUE) (`ind FM child` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST "F"
-- B6 / B7: only M insured; child with both, or with F only.
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind FM family` (`ind nonresident` "F") (`ind resident` "M") TRUE TRUE) (`ind FM child` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST "M"
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind FM family` (`ind nonresident` "F") (`ind resident` "M") TRUE FALSE) (`ind FM child` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST "M"
-- B8: neither insured.
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind FM family` (`ind nonresident` "F") (`ind nonresident` "M") TRUE TRUE) (`ind FM child` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- B9 / B10: three children with both parents; then the youngest with M only.
GIVEN mw3 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A family on a day`
`ind B9 family` mw3 MEANS
    `ind family` `ind usual day` (LIST `ind resident` "F", `ind resident` "M")
        (LIST `ind child` "K1" (YMD 2012 1 1) (LIST `ind natural father` "F" TRUE, `ind natural mother` "M" TRUE),
              `ind child` "K2" (YMD 2014 1 1) (LIST `ind natural father` "F" TRUE, `ind natural mother` "M" TRUE),
              `ind child` "K3" (YMD 2016 1 1) (LIST `ind natural father` "F" (NOT mw3), `ind natural mother` "M" TRUE))
#ASSERT `ind total` "F" (`ind at chosen` (`ind B9 family` FALSE)) EQUALS JUST 526
#ASSERT `ind total` "M" (`ind at chosen` (`ind B9 family` FALSE)) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `ind total` "F" (`ind at chosen` (`ind B9 family` TRUE)) EQUALS JUST 338
#ASSERT `ind total` "M" (`ind at chosen` (`ind B9 family` TRUE)) EQUALS JUST 150

-- B11 / B12: natural mother M and step-father S both insured; the natural father is not.
GIVEN mw IS A BOOLEAN, sw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A child`
`ind MS child` mw sw MEANS `ind child` "K" (YMD 2016 1 1) (LIST `ind natural mother` "M" mw, `ind step-father` "S" sw, `ind natural father` "NF" FALSE)
GIVEN mw IS A BOOLEAN, sw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A family on a day`
`ind MS family` mw sw MEANS `ind family` `ind usual day` (LIST `ind resident` "M", `ind resident` "S", `ind nonresident` "NF") (LIST `ind MS child` mw sw)
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind MS family` TRUE FALSE) (`ind MS child` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST "M"
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind MS family` FALSE TRUE) (`ind MS child` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST "S"

-- B13 / B14: two adoptive parents, both insured.
GIVEN fw IS A BOOLEAN, mw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A child`
`ind adopted child` fw mw MEANS `ind child` "AK" (YMD 2016 1 1) (LIST `ind adoptive father` "AF" fw, `ind adoptive mother` "AM" mw)
GIVEN fw IS A BOOLEAN, mw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A family on a day`
`ind adopted family` fw mw MEANS `ind family` `ind usual day` (LIST `ind resident` "AF", `ind resident` "AM") (LIST `ind adopted child` fw mw)
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind adopted family` TRUE TRUE) (`ind adopted child` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST "AF"
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind adopted family` FALSE TRUE) (`ind adopted child` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST "AM"

-- B15: "excluded father": F has s 121B income; child with both. In F's count; nobody is paid.
#ASSERT `ind whose count` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident with additional tax` "F") (`ind resident` "M") TRUE TRUE) (`ind FM child` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST "F"
#ASSERT `ind answer is` "F" (`ind at chosen` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident with additional tax` "F") (`ind resident` "M") TRUE TRUE)) `no child allowance, being an insured parent with income chargeable to additional tax`
#ASSERT `ind total` "M" (`ind at chosen` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident with additional tax` "F") (`ind resident` "M") TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS JUST 0
-- B16: the same, child with M only: M is paid 150.
#ASSERT `ind total` "M" (`ind at chosen` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident with additional tax` "F") (`ind resident` "M") FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS JUST 150

-- B17: natural mother M insured; insured grandmother G who supported the child; child with G only.
`ind B17 child` MEANS `ind child` "GC" (YMD 2016 1 1) (LIST `ind natural mother` "M" FALSE, `ind supporting grandmother` "G" TRUE TRUE)
`ind B17 family` MEANS `ind family` `ind usual day` (LIST `ind resident` "M", `ind resident` "G") (LIST `ind B17 child`)
#ASSERT `ind whose count` `ind B17 family` `ind B17 child` EQUALS JUST "G"

-- B18: s 67(a) holds, and the counts add up to the countable children (B10's family: 2 + 1 = 3).
#ASSERT `s 67(a) — no child is counted with more than one insured parent, in` (`ind B9 family` TRUE)
#ASSERT (`ind count` "F" (`ind at chosen` (`ind B9 family` TRUE)) PLUS `ind count` "M" (`ind at chosen` (`ind B9 family` TRUE))) EQUALS 3

§§ `C — the amount: s 68 and s 1 paragraph (2)`

-- Six children of P, born 2010 … 2020, all under 18 on the usual day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `A child`
`ind first n of six` n MEANS
    take n
        (LIST `ind P's child` "c1" (YMD 2010 1 1), `ind P's child` "c2" (YMD 2012 1 1), `ind P's child` "c3" (YMD 2014 1 1),
              `ind P's child` "c4" (YMD 2016 1 1), `ind P's child` "c5" (YMD 2018 1 1), `ind P's child` "c6" (YMD 2020 1 1))

GIVEN p IS A `A person`, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
`ind n children of` p n MEANS `ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` p (`ind first n of six` n))

-- C0-C6: totals by count.
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind n children of` (`ind resident` "P") 0) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind n children of` (`ind resident` "P") 1) EQUALS JUST 150
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind n children of` (`ind resident` "P") 2) EQUALS JUST 338
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind n children of` (`ind resident` "P") 3) EQUALS JUST 526
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind n children of` (`ind resident` "P") 4) EQUALS JUST 714
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind n children of` (`ind resident` "P") 5) EQUALS JUST 864
