§§ `F — where the source does not answer`

-- F1: two insured mothers (one natural, one adoptive), child with both.
`ind F1 child` MEANS `ind child` "K" (YMD 2016 1 1) (LIST `ind natural mother` "M1" TRUE, `ind adoptive mother` "M2" TRUE)
`ind F1 family` MEANS `ind family` `ind usual day` (LIST `ind resident` "M1", `ind resident` "M2") (LIST `ind F1 child`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind whose count, forced` `ind F1 family` `ind F1 child`
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind at chosen` `ind F1 family`

-- F2 / F3: natural mother M and step-father S both insured; child with both / with neither.
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind whose count, forced` (`ind MS family` TRUE TRUE) (`ind MS child` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind at chosen` (`ind MS family` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind whose count, forced` (`ind MS family` FALSE FALSE) (`ind MS child` FALSE FALSE)

-- F4: F insured, M not insured, child with M only. Expected: refusal (the text does not choose).
-- FAILS (finding 1): the encoding answers JUST "F" (its fork F7).
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind whose count, forced` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident` "F") (`ind nonresident` "M") FALSE TRUE) (`ind FM child` FALSE TRUE)

-- F5: the insured father has children by more than one woman (s 69A).
