#ASSERT REFUSED `ind at chosen` (`ind FM family` (`ind resident man with children by several women` "F") (`ind resident` "M") TRUE TRUE)

-- F6: the only parent was insured and has ceased to be (s 71).
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind formerly insured` "P") (LIST `ind A1 child`))

-- F8: born 29 February 2008: 2026-02-27 under 18; 2026-03-01 not; 2026-02-28 the law does not say (expected: refusal).
`ind leap child` MEANS `ind P's child` "leap" (YMD 2008 2 29)
#ASSERT `s 65 — under 18 on` (YMD 2026 2 27) `:` `ind leap child`
#ASSERT NOT `s 65 — under 18 on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `:` `ind leap child`
-- FAILS (finding 2): the encoding clamps the anniversary to 28 February, total 0 (its fork F2).
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind at chosen` (`ind single` (YMD 2026 2 28) (`ind resident` "P") (LIST `ind leap child`))

-- F9: a six-month trip (left 2026-01-10, back 2026-07-10); a day in its first month. Expected: refusal,
-- whether or not the return day is known when the question is asked.
-- FAILS (finding 3): with the return day supplied the encoding answers "abroad", total 0 (its fork F3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind one child away` (YMD 2026 2 1) (`ind absence` (YMD 2026 1 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 7 10))) FALSE
-- FAILS (finding 3): with no return day the encoding answers "in Israel", total 150 (its fork F3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind one child away` (YMD 2026 2 1) (`ind absence` (YMD 2026 1 10) NOTHING) FALSE

-- F10: the mother is a resident "housewife" within s 238, not insured under Chapter 11. Expected: refusal.
-- FAILS (finding 4): the encoding answers "not being an insured parent"; no fork recorded.
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind resident housewife` "P") (LIST `ind A1 child`))

-- F11: natural father, natural mother and step-father all insured; child with M and S.
`ind F11 child` MEANS `ind child` "K" (YMD 2016 1 1) (LIST `ind natural father` "F" FALSE, `ind natural mother` "M" TRUE, `ind step-father` "S" TRUE)
`ind F11 family` MEANS `ind family` `ind usual day` (LIST `ind resident` "F", `ind resident` "M", `ind resident` "S") (LIST `ind F11 child`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind whose count, forced` `ind F11 family` `ind F11 child`

§§ `X — added after reading the encoding's interface (not in DECIDED-ANSWERS; licensed by the same source text)`

-- X1 (other side of A4): a resident whose absence the authorised employee does NOT think a reasonable
-- temporary absence is not insured under s 65(a)(2) (line 803 "ואינו נעדר ממנה אלא העדר ארעי שהוא סביר").
#ASSERT `ind total` "P" (`ind at chosen` (`ind single` `ind usual day` (`ind resident absent beyond a reasonable absence` "P") (LIST `ind A1 child`))) EQUALS JUST 0

-- X2: a child who was abroad five months and came back before the day is in Israel on the day
-- (s 65 line 807 "ובלבד שהילד נמצא בישראל"). If the caller supplies that finished absence, the answer
-- should be either "counted" or a rejected fact (the noun says the absence must be the one in
-- progress on the day), never a silent "abroad".
`ind X2 result` MEANS `ind one child away` (YMD 2026 9 1) (`ind absence` (YMD 2026 1 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10))) FALSE
-- FAILS (finding 5): the encoding counts the child as abroad after the return, total 0, facts not rejected.
#ASSERT (`ind total` "P" `ind X2 result` EQUALS JUST 150) OR `ind rejected` `ind X2 result`
